Ladybird takes the view box of an SVG view specification in an SVG
image’s URL fragment as the active view, and ignores a specification
that names an attribute twice, as the spec’s “each type may only occur
at most one time in a correctly formed SVGViewSpec” requires. Gecko does
the same: Its SVGFragmentIdentifier ProcessViewSpecAttr() rejects a
repeated attribute. But Blink and WebKit let a repeated attribute
replace the earlier one, in SVGViewSpec::ParseViewSpecInternal() and
SVGViewSpec::parseViewSpec(). And all three apply the specification’s
preserveAspectRatio and transform, which Ladybird doesn’t yet.
